     "data": {
      "text/markdown": [
       "Yes—AI coding-agent harnesses. For **August 17–23, 2026**, the noteworthy developments are:\n",
       "\n",
       "- **Codex shipped reliability improvements:** sessions can reconnect through temporary provider outages, while MCP servers recover after OAuth reauthentication without requiring a restart. [Codex releases](https://github.com/openai/codex/releases)\n",
       "- **Claude Code’s recent release line centers on Sonnet 5:** it became the default model, with a native 1M-token context window. Anthropic also improved subagent summaries, API retry feedback, syntax highlighting, and GitHub App installation. [Claude Code changelog](https://github.com/anthropics/claude-code/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md)\n",
       "- **OpenCode continued its rapid cadence:** versions `1.18.10`, `1.18.11`, and `1.18.12` appeared during the week, reinforcing its position as the fast-moving, model-agnostic alternative. [OpenCode packages](https://github.com/anomalyco/opencode/pkgs/container/opencode/versions)\n",
       "- **Harness choice itself became the conversation:** a widely discussed community comparison claimed up to a **7× cost difference at similar quality** when the same model was run through Claude Code, Codex, OpenCode, and Pi. Treat this as an interesting community experiment—not an independently validated benchmark. [Discussion](https://www.reddit.com/r/PiCodingAgent/comments/1vqs0c7/i_ran_the_same_model_through_claude_code_codex/)\n",
       "- **Local-model users increasingly favor interchangeable harnesses:** this week’s discussions emphasized OpenCode and Pi for model flexibility, while Claude Code and Codex remain attractive for more polished, integrated experiences. [Community poll](https://www.reddit.com/r/LocalLLM/comments/1vrsi3r/best_harness_for_coding_with_local_llm_pi/)\n",
       "\n",
       "**Bottom line:** there was no single blockbuster harness launch this week. The trend is toward **resilient sessions, longer context, stronger subagent coordination, and separating the model from the harness** when evaluating quality and cost.\n"
      ]
